IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-test-conduct`

-- g5-tests-test-conduct.l4: tests of g5-test-conduct.l4 (ss.37 and 38).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.37 and 38 (inputs/law.wiki lines 306 to 322) BEFORE any of
-- this was run.  A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so the rules are exercised with #TRACE, each with its
-- expected result written above it as `-- EXPECT:` and checked by work/g5/tracecheck.py.

§ `Tests of ss 37 and 38`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- Tester or expert at work: capacity, authorisation in force, acting for an auxiliary test, acting to give an opinion,
-- within the conditions of the instrument, the Law has commenced for the work
--                                                               capacity               in force  test   opinion  within
`a tester doing an auxiliary test`          MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE, TRUE
`a tester who is only giving an opinion`    MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,   TRUE, TRUE
`an expert giving an opinion`               MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as an expert`, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,   TRUE, TRUE
`an expert doing an auxiliary test`         MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as an expert`, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE, TRUE
`an expert doing neither`                   MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as an expert`, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE,  TRUE, TRUE
`a tester whose authorisation is not in force` MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE, TRUE
`a tester outside the conditions of his instrument` MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a tester where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Entry: the senior inspector's reason (limb 1, limb 2); showed the instrument; written consent; told the purpose; told the
-- right to refuse; told the right to withdraw; told before consenting; withdrew consent; a dwelling; the holder asked; arranged
--                                                                   limb1  limb2  showed  consent  purpose  refuse  withdraw  before  withdrew  dwelling  asked  arranged
`a proper entry to a workshop`                 MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a proper entry on the engager limb`           MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an entry with no reason to suppose`           MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an entry without showing the instrument`      MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an entry without written consent`             MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an entry where the purpose was not explained` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an entry where the right to refuse was not explained` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an entry where the right to withdraw was not explained` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an entry where the explanation came after the consent` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an entry after the holder withdrew his consent` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a proper entry to a dwelling`                 MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE,   TRUE,  TRUE
`a dwelling entry the holder did not ask for`  MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE,   FALSE, TRUE
`a dwelling entry not arranged in advance`     MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE,  TRUE,   TRUE,  FALSE
`a dwelling entry with neither request nor arrangement` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a workshop entry with a request and an arrangement nobody needed` MEANS `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

§§ `s 37 -- Acts of testers and experts`

-- Lead-in (src:307): a tester for an auxiliary test; an expert for an auxiliary test or an opinion.
#ASSERT `s 37(a) — the purpose fits the capacity` `a tester doing an auxiliary test`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the purpose fits the capacity` `a tester who is only giving an opinion`
#ASSERT `s 37(a) — the purpose fits the capacity` `an expert giving an opinion`
#ASSERT `s 37(a) — the purpose fits the capacity` `an expert doing an auxiliary test`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the purpose fits the capacity` `an expert doing neither`
#ASSERT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `a tester doing an auxiliary test`
#ASSERT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `an expert giving an opinion`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `a tester who is only giving an opinion`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `an expert doing neither`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `a tester outside the conditions of his instrument`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a) — the tester or expert holds the power: authorised, acting for a purpose that fits his capacity, within the conditions of his instrument, the Law having commenced for the work` `a tester where the Law has not yet commenced for the work`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester where the Law has not yet commenced for the work` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT `s 37 — the party acting as` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` EQUALS `a tester`
#ASSERT `s 37 — the party acting as` `an expert giving an opinion` EQUALS `an expert`

-- s.37(a)(1) (src:308): the SENIOR inspector's reason to suppose, on either limb.
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the senior inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the senior inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `a proper entry on the engager limb`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the senior inspector has reason to suppose that unlicensed or non-conforming work is done or engaged there` `an entry with no reason to suppose`

-- s.37(b) (src:313-317): each of the four conditions, alone.
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(1) — the tester or expert showed his instrument of authorisation to the holder of the place` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(1) — the tester or expert showed his instrument of authorisation to the holder of the place` `an entry without showing the instrument`
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(2) — the holder gave written consent to the entry, and it stands` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(2) — the holder gave written consent to the entry, and it stands` `an entry without written consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(3) — before consenting the holder was told the purpose of the tests and of his rights to refuse and to withdraw consent` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(3) — before consenting the holder was told the purpose of the tests and of his rights to refuse and to withdraw consent` `an entry where the purpose was not explained`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(3) — before consenting the holder was told the purpose of the tests and of his rights to refuse and to withdraw consent` `an entry where the right to refuse was not explained`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(3) — before consenting the holder was told the purpose of the tests and of his rights to refuse and to withdraw consent` `an entry where the right to withdraw was not explained`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(3) — before consenting the holder was told the purpose of the tests and of his rights to refuse and to withdraw consent` `an entry where the explanation came after the consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a proper entry to a dwelling`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a dwelling entry the holder did not ask for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a dwelling entry not arranged in advance`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a dwelling entry with neither request nor arrangement`
-- A request and an arrangement nobody needed for a workshop do no harm.
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(4) — a dwelling is entered only at the holder's request and by prior arrangement` `a workshop entry with a request and an arrangement nobody needed`

-- s.37(b) as a whole: all four.
#ASSERT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `a proper entry to a dwelling`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry without showing the instrument`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry without written consent`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry where the purpose was not explained`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `a dwelling entry the holder did not ask for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `a dwelling entry not arranged in advance`

-- Fork F-WITHDRAW: a consent the holder withdrew before the tests began no longer stands; the alternative ignores it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b)(2) — the holder gave written consent to the entry, and it stands` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(2), withdrawal ignored — the holder gave written consent to the entry` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b) — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(b), withdrawal ignored — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(b), withdrawal ignored — all the conditions of entry are met` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(b), withdrawal ignored — all the conditions of entry are met` `an entry without written consent`

-- Entry as a whole (s.37(a)(1) with (b)): the power, the senior inspector's reason, the four conditions.
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `an expert giving an opinion` `a proper entry to a dwelling`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry with no reason to suppose`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry without written consent`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a dwelling entry the holder did not ask for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester who is only giving an opinion` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester outside the conditions of his instrument` `a proper entry to a workshop`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(1) — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(1), withdrawal ignored — the tester or expert may enter the place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(1) — a tester or expert may enter a place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a proper entry to a workshop` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(1) — a tester or expert may enter a place` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry without written consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(1) — a tester or expert may enter a place` `an expert giving an opinion` `a proper entry to a dwelling` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2
-- "Only if all of these": entering without them is a breach by whoever acts.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `a tester`
#TRACE `s 37(b) — a tester or expert shall not enter a place unless all the conditions are met` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an entry without written consent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an expert`
#TRACE `s 37(b) — a tester or expert shall not enter a place unless all the conditions are met` `an expert doing an auxiliary test` `a dwelling entry not arranged in advance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(b) — a tester or expert shall not enter a place unless all the conditions are met` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a proper entry to a workshop` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `enter a place for the purpose of auxiliary tests or an expert opinion` AT 2

-- s.37(a)(2) (src:309): the demand for name, address and identification is addressed to a person doing the work.
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(2) — the tester or expert may require the person doing the work to give his name and address and to show identification` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(2) — the tester or expert may require the person doing the work to give his name and address and to show identification` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(2) — the tester or expert may require the person doing the work to give his name and address and to show identification` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force` TRUE
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(2) — a tester or expert may require a person doing work on a cooling system to give his name and address and to show identification` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `require the person doing the work to give his name and address and to show identification` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(2) — a tester or expert may require a person doing work on a cooling system to give his name and address and to show identification` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `require the person doing the work to give his name and address and to show identification` AT 2

-- s.37(a)(3) (src:310): the checklist the senior inspector set; publication is a separate duty on the reading taken.
-- Checklist: set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test, published in Reshumot and on the Ministry website
`a published checklist`   MEANS `Checklist used by a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  TRUE
`an unpublished checklist` MEANS `Checklist used by a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  FALSE
`a list the senior inspector did not set` MEANS `Checklist used by a tester or an expert` OF FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(3) — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a published checklist`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(3) — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an unpublished checklist`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(3) — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a list the senior inspector did not set`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(3) — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force` `a published checklist`
-- Fork F-PUBLISH: read as a condition of use, publication is needed.
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(3), publication read as a condition of use — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a published checklist`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(3), publication read as a condition of use — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an unpublished checklist`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(3) — a tester or expert may use a checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an unpublished checklist` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `use a checklist` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(3) — a tester or expert may use a checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a list the senior inspector did not set` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `use a checklist` AT 2
-- The publication duty: the inferred publisher is the senior inspector; the other inference is callable.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(3) — the senior inspector shall have the checklist published in Reshumot and on the Ministry website` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the senior inspector` DOES `publish the checklist in Reshumot and on the Ministry website` AT 12
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(3) — the senior inspector shall have the checklist published in Reshumot and on the Ministry website` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(3) — the checklist shall be published in Reshumot and on the Ministry website by` `the Ministry` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `publish the checklist in Reshumot and on the Ministry website` AT 12

-- s.37(a)(4) (src:311): receive from a person concerned what appears in the checklist; not "require".
`a request for what the checklist lists, from a person concerned` MEANS `Request for documents or information under a checklist` OF TRUE, TRUE
`a request for something the checklist does not list`            MEANS `Request for documents or information under a checklist` OF TRUE, FALSE
`a request to a person not concerned`                            MEANS `Request for documents or information under a checklist` OF FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(4) — the documents or information may be received: the person is concerned and they appear in the checklist` `a request for what the checklist lists, from a person concerned`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(4) — the documents or information may be received: the person is concerned and they appear in the checklist` `a request for something the checklist does not list`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(4) — the documents or information may be received: the person is concerned and they appear in the checklist` `a request to a person not concerned`
#ASSERT `s 37(a)(4) — the tester or expert may receive the documents or information` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a request for what the checklist lists, from a person concerned`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(4) — the tester or expert may receive the documents or information` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a request for something the checklist does not list`
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(4) — the tester or expert may receive the documents or information` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force` `a request for what the checklist lists, from a person concerned`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(4) — a tester or expert may receive from a person concerned the documents or information in the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a request for what the checklist lists, from a person concerned` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `receive from a person concerned the documents or information that appear in the checklist` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(4) — a tester or expert may receive from a person concerned the documents or information in the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `a request to a person not concerned` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `receive from a person concerned the documents or information that appear in the checklist` AT 2

-- s.37(a)(5) (src:312): tests on a cooling system.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(5) — a tester or expert may carry out tests on a cooling system` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `carry out tests on a cooling system` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 37(a)(5) — a tester or expert may carry out tests on a cooling system` `a tester whose authorisation is not in force` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `carry out tests on a cooling system` AT 2
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 37(a)(5) — a tester or expert may carry out tests on a cooling system` `an expert giving an opinion` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `use a power of a tester or an expert` `carry out tests on a cooling system` AT 2

§§ `s 38 -- Information security and confidentiality`

-- Measures: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open
--                                                       misuse  access  systems  other
`measures that secure the information`       MEANS `Measures securing information under section 38(a)` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`measures that leave misuse open`            MEANS `Measures securing information under section 38(a)` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`measures that leave access uncontrolled`    MEANS `Measures securing information under section 38(a)` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`measures that leave the computer systems open` MEANS `Measures securing information under section 38(a)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`measures that leave another aspect open`    MEANS `Measures securing information under section 38(a)` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(a) — the measures secure the information: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open` `measures that secure the information`
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(a) — the measures secure the information: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open` `measures that leave misuse open`
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(a) — the measures secure the information: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open` `measures that leave access uncontrolled`
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(a) — the measures secure the information: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open` `measures that leave the computer systems open`
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(a) — the measures secure the information: misuse prevented, access and use controlled, computer systems secured, nothing else left open` `measures that leave another aspect open`

`an engagement made in accordance with section 34(c)` MEANS `Engagement for information security` OF TRUE
`an engagement not made in accordance with section 34(c)` MEANS `Engagement for information security` OF FALSE
`securing the information fully` MEANS `secure the information received in the course of an act under the engagement` `measures that secure the information`
`securing the information with misuse left open` MEANS `secure the information received in the course of an act under the engagement` `measures that leave misuse open`

-- s.38(a) (src:320): an engaged body or expert is responsible; the duty is discharged by securing the information.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(a) — an engaged testing body shall secure the information` `an engagement made in accordance with section 34(c)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `securing the information fully` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(a) — an engaged testing body shall secure the information` `an engagement made in accordance with section 34(c)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `securing the information with misuse left open` AT 3
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(a) — an engaged expert shall secure the information` `an engagement made in accordance with section 34(c)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `securing the information fully` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(a) — an engaged expert shall secure the information` `an engagement made in accordance with section 34(c)` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- Not engaged under (c): no duty under (a).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(a) — an engaged testing body shall secure the information` `an engagement not made in accordance with section 34(c)` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)

-- s.38(b) (src:321): at the end of an engagement as in (a): hand over, destroy what remains, tell the senior inspector.
-- End of an engagement: made under (c), has ended, information remains after the hand-over
`an ended engagement with information remaining` MEANS `End of an engagement under section 38(b)` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`an ended engagement with nothing remaining`     MEANS `End of an engagement under section 38(b)` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an engagement still running`                    MEANS `End of an engagement under section 38(b)` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an ended engagement made without a tender`      MEANS `End of an engagement under section 38(b)` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
-- The three steps in order: FULFILLED.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement with information remaining` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `hand the information to the senior inspector` AT 2
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `destroy the information that remains` AT 4
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `tell the senior inspector that the information was destroyed` AT 5
-- Handed over and nothing remained: done.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement with nothing remaining` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `hand the information to the senior inspector` AT 2
-- Handed over, something remained and nothing more was done: the duty to destroy stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement with information remaining` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `hand the information to the senior inspector` AT 2
-- Destroyed but not told: the duty to tell stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement with information remaining` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `hand the information to the senior inspector` AT 2
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `destroy the information that remains` AT 4
-- Nothing done: the duty to hand over stands (no time is stated).
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement with information remaining` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- The engagement has not ended, or was not made under (c): no duty.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an engagement still running` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(b) — a testing body at the end of its engagement` `an ended engagement made without a tender` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- The expert's version is the same rule with the expert as the party.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(b) — an expert at the end of his engagement` `an ended engagement with information remaining` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `hand the information to the senior inspector` AT 2
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `destroy the information that remains` AT 4
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `tell the senior inspector that the information was destroyed` AT 5

-- s.38(c) (src:322): no disclosure or use except to carry out the act; for good (no time stated).
`information obtained in an act under an engagement` MEANS `Information obtained by a tester, an expert or a testing body` OF TRUE
`information obtained otherwise` MEANS `Information obtained by a tester, an expert or a testing body` OF FALSE
-- A disclosure or use: in order to perform the act; required by the Law under s.34(d), 34(e) or 38(b)
`a disclosure for another purpose` MEANS `disclose or use information obtained in an act under the engagement` FALSE FALSE
`a use to carry out the act` MEANS `disclose or use information obtained in an act under the engagement` TRUE FALSE
`a hand-over the Law requires` MEANS `disclose or use information obtained in an act under the engagement` FALSE TRUE
-- Fork F-DISCLOSE: read literally the exception covers only carrying out the act, so a hand-over the Law itself orders is caught.
#ASSERT `s 38(c) — the disclosure or use is permitted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(c) — the disclosure or use is permitted` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(c) — the disclosure or use is permitted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(c) — the disclosure or use is permitted` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(c), literally — the disclosure or use is permitted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(c), literally — the disclosure or use is permitted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(c), literally — the disclosure or use is permitted` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(c), literally — the disclosure or use is permitted` FALSE FALSE
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `a testing body`
#TRACE `s 38(c) — a testing body shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 30
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(c) — a testing body shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `a use to carry out the act` AT 30
-- A disclosure the Law itself requires (the hand-over of s.38(b), the reports of s.34(d), (e)) is not caught.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 38(c) — a testing body shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `a hand-over the Law requires` AT 30
-- The prohibition does not lapse with time.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `a tester`
#TRACE `s 38(c) — a tester shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 4001
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `an expert`
#TRACE `s 38(c) — an expert shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 30
-- Information that did not come from an act under the engagement is outside (c).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(c) — a testing body shall not disclose or use the information` `information obtained otherwise` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 30
-- An employee who is not a tester is bound (the party stands in as `a person`); a stranger is not.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `a person`
#TRACE `s 38(c) — an employee of a testing body who is not a tester shall not disclose or use the information` TRUE `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 30
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 38(c) — an employee of a testing body who is not a tester shall not disclose or use the information` FALSE `information obtained in an act under an engagement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person` DOES `a disclosure for another purpose` AT 30
